  "prefLabel": "Agr 1003.01 Apples",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Agr 1003.01 Apples. The following requirements shall apply for use of the seal of quality design on apples:\n\n(a) A packer of New Hampshire apples may use the state of New Hampshire seal of quality design after receiving a yearly permit from the department, and only while said yearly permit is active;\n\n(b) A packer of New Hampshire apples shall only use the state of New Hampshire seal of quality design on apples in compliance with RSA 426:11-12, Agr 901, and Agr 1003;\n\n(c) Apples shall be marked in accordance with the provisions of the U.S. Standards for Grades of Apples; 7 CFR, Section 51.300-51.322, effective October 31, 2019;\n\n(d) Apples shall meet the requirements of one of the following grades, and associated color and tolerances, as specified in U.S. Standards for Grades of Apples, 7 CFR, Section 51.300-51.322, effective October 31, 2019:\n\n(1) U.S. Extra Fancy;\n\n(2) U.S. Fancy; or\n\n(3) Combination of U.S. Extra Fancy and U.S. Fancy;\n\n(e) Apples shall meet the “Condition After Storage” or “Transit Standards” as specified in the U.S. Standards for Grades of Apples, 7 CFR, Section 51.300-51.322, effective October 31, 2019; and\n\n(f) Apples shall be packaged in accordance with the “Packing Requirements” standards as specified in the U.S. Standards for Grades of Apples, 7 CFR, Section 51.300-51.322, effective October 31, 2019.\n\nSource. #6734, eff 4-21-98 (from Agr 1002.01), EXPIRED: 4-21-06\n\nNew. #10952, eff 10-21-15; ss by #14554, eff 4-7-26, EXPIRES: 4-7-36",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/agr1000.html"
